# TODO - DOOM quality and modernization pass

## Objective

Consume the user-supplied source tree under ignored `doom/` and use
`interop/algorithms/quality/main.rs` to produce a deterministic normalized source tree
under `interop/algorithms/quality/out/doom_fixed/`. Repair repeated `tools/tidy`
diagnostic families through reusable AST transformations, modernize explicit
platform adapters, and preserve behavior and required provenance before any
translation units are amalgamated.

## Current implementation

- `interop/algorithms/quality/main.rs` owns the quality-first transformation
  boundary; automatic AST rewrite families remain incomplete.
- Repository-root `doom/` is the untouched local baseline. The ignored
  `interop/algorithms/quality/in/doom/` tree is the manually modernized
  development oracle used to discover reusable transformations.
- `interop/algorithms/quality/comparison/generate.py` compares those corpora with
  pinned LLVM 22.1.8 quality gates, records source and asset hashes, and fails
  closed if either live corpus changes during a measurement.
- The current coherent snapshot records 143,662 unique findings in the baseline
  and 41,162 in the development oracle. This is progress evidence, not
  acceptance: zero applicable findings and reproducible generation into
  `out/doom_fixed/` remain required.

## Acceptance

- The user-owned input tree is never modified; all generated normalized source
  lives under `interop/algorithms/quality/out/doom_fixed/`.
- Repeated linter failures become reusable semantics-aware transformations; no
  blanket suppression or source-specific hand patch remains necessary.
- Video, input, timing, audio, game-data, resolution, and frame-rate support are
  represented through explicit adapters and measured behavior rather than hidden
  host substitutions.
- Differential native tests compare admitted original behavior with each
  behavior-affecting generated stage and record intentional fixes separately.
- Legal/provenance comments required by upstream material survive comment cleanup.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `doom/`, `interop/algorithms/quality/`,
  `interop/adapters/`, `interop/algorithms/quality/out/doom_fixed/`, `tools/tidy/`.
- Current comparison evidence: `interop/algorithms/quality/comparison/` contains
  the deterministic generator, aggregate metrics, and compact LaTeX report.
- Required evidence: deterministic source manifests, linter reports,
  transformation provenance, native differential traces, and adapter tests.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `clang-c-frontend-integration`,
  `tools-tidy-lowerability-contract`, `supported-libc-contract`,
  `reuse-shar-legal-and-interoperability-corpus`.
